---
import StudioLayout from '../layouts/StudioLayout.astro';
import '../styles/boutique.css';
const FAB_URL = 'https://www.fab.com/listings/47a56c00-ab32-4c20-8aba-04935b4a2578';
const schema = [{
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  '@id': 'https://strategicsloth.com/focusrail/#app',
  name: 'Focusrail',
  applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
  applicationSubCategory: 'Unreal Engine plugin',
  operatingSystem: 'Unreal Engine 5',
  description: 'Controller and keyboard navigation for Unreal Engine UMG: author focus rails in the widget editor, see focus at runtime, and validate navigation with Focus Doctor.',
  author: { '@id': 'https://strategicsloth.com/#studio' },
  publisher: { '@id': 'https://strategicsloth.com/#studio' },
  url: 'https://strategicsloth.com/focusrail/',
  sameAs: [FAB_URL]
}];
---
<StudioLayout title="Focusrail: UMG Controller Navigation Plugin for Unreal | Strategic Sloth" description="Author, debug and validate controller and keyboard focus in Unreal Engine 5 UMG. Focus rails in the widget editor, plus Focus Doctor to flag dead ends. On Fab." schema={schema}>
<section class="b-intro container">
  <p class="eyebrow">Unreal Engine 5 · UMG · C++ plugin</p>
  <h1>Focusrail:<br><em>controller navigation that holds up.</em></h1>
  <p class="lede">Author, debug and validate controller and keyboard focus in Unreal Engine 5 UMG. Draw focus rails directly in the widget editor, see focus at runtime, and run Focus Doctor to find dead ends before your players do.</p>
  <div class="b-hero-actions"><a class="button" href={FAB_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on Fab <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/services/unreal/commonui/">CommonUI setup & focus <span>→</span></a></div>
</section>

<section class="b-section container">
  <div class="b-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">IN THE EDITOR</p><h2>Rails you can see.<br><em>Validation you can trust.</em></h2></div><p>Built for the way Unreal UI teams work.</p></div>
  <div class="b-gallery">
    <figure><img src="/media/services/unreal-focus-doctor.webp" alt="Unreal Engine widget designer with the Focusrail Focus Doctor panel reporting a duplicate navigation order and offering an automatic fix" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Focus Doctor validating a widget’s navigation rail and flagging a duplicate order.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="/media/work/focusrail-runtime.webp" alt="A running Unreal pause menu with the Focusrail overlay naming the focused Resume button and its next and previous targets" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Runtime overlay naming the focused widget and where focus goes next.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><img src="/media/services/portfolio/ue-widget-editor.webp" alt="Unreal Engine widget blueprint editor with palette, hierarchy and a numbered focus rail drawn over four menu buttons" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Rails authored in the UMG widget editor.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="b-sage b-section container">
  <div class="b-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHY IT EXISTS</p><h2>Where UMG often breaks.</h2></div><p>Controller focus and input routing are the most common reasons Unreal menus feel broken. Focusrail makes both visible and testable.</p></div>
  <ul class="b-list b-list-2">
    <li><strong>Focus memory</strong><span>Remembering where focus was on a layer</span></li>
    <li><strong>Popup lifecycle</strong><span>Predictable focus on open, return and close</span></li>
    <li><strong>Input conflicts</strong><span>When mouse hover fights gamepad focus</span></li>
    <li><strong>Scroll & grids</strong><span>No traps, no skips</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p class="b-note">Note: price, supported versions and CommonUI compatibility are listed on Fab.</p>
</section>
</StudioLayout>
